      "text": "To solve the problem of finding how many odd numbers between \\( 100 \\) and \\( 999 \\) have distinct digits, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify all 3-digit odd numbers:** \n   An odd number must end in one of the digits \\(1, 3, 5, 7,\\) or \\(9\\).\n\n2. **Exclude numbers with repeated digits:** In a three-digit number where digits need to be distinct, there are two scenarios to consider:\n   - The hundreds digit, tens digit, and units digit are all distinct.\n   - At least one digit is repeated.\n\nWe will calculate the number of valid odd numbers following these criteria.\n\n### Step-by-Step Calculation:\n\n1. **Case 1: All digits are distinct:**\n   - The units digit can be any of \\(1, 3, 5, 7, 9\\) (5 choices).\n   - The hundreds digit can be any digit from 1 to 9 except the one chosen for the units digit (8 choices).\n   - The tens digit can be any digit from 0 to 9 except the ones already chosen (7 or 8 choices).\n\n   So, the total number of three-digit numbers beginning with a distinct digit is:\n   \\[\n   5 \\times 8 \\times 7 = 280\n   \\]\n\n2. **Case 2: Repeat one of the digits:**\n   - We will now consider each case where one digit is repeated:\n     - If the repeating digit is in the hundreds or tens place, then there are 4 choices for the repeating digit (since it cannot be 0).\n     - The third digit is the remaining digit (6 options).\n\n     For hundreds tens place:\n     \\[\n     5 \\times 6 - \\text{(numbers with repeated 0 in the hundreds place)}\n     \\]\n     There are 25 such numbers (5 choices for the tens digit, 4 choices for the hundreds digit different from 0, and 1 choice for the remaining digit).\n\n     For tens hundreds place:\n     \\[\n     6 \\times 5 = 30\n     \\]\n\n     Thus, the total number of numbers where one digit appears twice is:\n     \\[\n     5 \\times 6 - 25 + 6 \\times 5 = 30\n     \\]\n\n3. **Adding both cases together:**\n   \\[\n   280 + 30 = 310\n   \\]\n\nThus, the number of odd numbers between \\(100\\) and \\(999\\) with distinct digits is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{310}\n\\]",
